\subsection{Preprocessing requirements}{

Factor/categorical predictors need to be converted to numeric values
(e.g., dummy or indicator variables) for this engine. When using the
formula method via \code{\link[=fit.model_spec]{fit()}}, parsnip will
convert factor columns to indicators.

The \code{x} engine argument names penalized predictor columns after
preprocessing. For factor predictors, use the names of the generated
indicator columns.

\code{ordinalgmifs::ordinalgmifs()} centers and scales penalized predictors
by default; set the native \code{scale} argument through \code{set_engine()} to
change this.
}

\subsection{Case weights}{

